# Git — Conflicts & Recovery

Created: 2026-02-02 05:37 UTC  
Last reviewed: 2026-02-02 05:37 UTC

## Resolve Conflicts During Rebase
```sh
git status
# resolve files
git add -A
git rebase --continue
```

Abort if you need to start over:
```sh
git rebase --abort
```

## Resolve Conflicts During Merge
```sh
git status
# resolve files
git add -A
git commit
```

Abort a merge:
```sh
git merge --abort
```

## Restore a File to `main`
```sh
git restore --source=origin/main -- path/to/file
```

## Undo a Commit (Preferred: Revert)
Use revert when history is already shared.
```sh
git revert <sha>
```

## Find “What Changed This Line”
```sh
git blame -L <start>,<end> path/to/file
git show <sha>
```

